=269\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the magnitude is\n\n$$\n|a+b|=\\sqrt{269}=\\sqrt{269}\n$$\n\nand the corresponding unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u&=\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|}\\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{269}}(a+b)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502475 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5187951d-7851-587d-950c-40bb153d472f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{25}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502469} {:answer/id #uuid "6e2a4a21-5bb0-58a1-947a-94a1e48e9040" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{31}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502477} {:answer/id #uuid "8db1a6cd-dc5f-5a94-827b-105391468bba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{24}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502491} {:answer/id #uuid "b2829203-bf6a-5c53-a2c3-4e8f9c2d513b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{625}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502505} {:answer/id #uuid "d27c1ed4-497a-5760-94ef-c9d5868e78f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502514}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502469} :answer-field/id #uuid "2aef0246-9ad6-53c6-bd16-842273614654" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502445}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6590a604-4765-5f8b-a2e2-8d63f022789c" :question/problem "The vector $a$ is directed horizontally to the right and has magnitude $7$, while the vector $b$ is directed vertically down and has magnitude $24$. Which of the following is a unit vector that is parallel to $a + b$?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/worked-solution "First, we have to find $a+b$. The given directions are perpendicular, so the triangle law of addition gives a right triangle.\n\nTo find the unit vector corresponding to $a+b$, we have to divide by the magnitude:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|}\n$$\n\nTo find the magnitude, we can use the Pythagorean theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a+b|^2&=|a|^2+|b|^2\\\\\n&=7^2+24^2\\\\\n&=49+576\\\\\n&=625\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the magnitude is\n\n$$\n|a+b|=\\sqrt{625}=25\n$$\n\nand the corresponding unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u&=\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|}\\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{25}(a+b)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502480 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f765063-d719-52c4-8758-d060bda218f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{17}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502435} {:answer/id #uuid "32560453-68cf-58ec-bcc4-5600e1322729" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{169}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502452} {:answer/id #uuid "41d57afd-d376-56ab-93c1-98b7ac6b90ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502460} {:answer/id #uuid "77ff5108-e30a-53d5-be88-86070273ff49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502483} {:answer/id #uuid "fc0d9ba2-7b90-5e41-9a61-466e727688ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{13}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502533}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502533} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b249dbc-2bf2-5899-a0d2-ee75f2b3d61f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502446}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7322374e-92d3-521a-9be7-e4d802ea5343" :question/problem "The vector $a$ is directed horizontally to the right and has magnitude $5$, while the vector $b$ is directed vertically down and has magnitude $12$. Which of the following is a unit vector that is parallel to $a + b$?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/worked-solution "First, we have to find $a+b$. The given directions are perpendicular, so the triangle law of addition gives a right triangle.\n\nTo find the unit vector corresponding to $a+b$, we have to divide by the magnitude:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|}\n$$\n\nTo find the magnitude, we can use the Pythagorean theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a+b|^2&=|a|^2+|b|^2\\\\\n&=5^2+12^2\\\\\n&=25+144\\\\\n&=169\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the magnitude is\n\n$$\n|a+b|=\\sqrt{169}=13\n$$\n\nand the corresponding unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u&=\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|}\\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{13}(a+b)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502481 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23367339-2bec-5fb2-b0d6-1b8facee4403" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{29}}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502443} {:answer/id #uuid "83c935e8-1d5d-5e5f-8318-46aace00fc74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502488} {:answer/id #uuid "a1ba17d7-9149-54a0-86fb-5eaf7fb69c50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502498} {:answer/id #uuid "a7d95cee-ac5e-53ac-aac6-cd15a27bdd93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502501} {:answer/id #uuid "be4619ed-0646-5ce6-bd3b-54760cc6c1de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{29}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502508}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502443} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcc7f93a-2ca9-55fc-98df-078a1b8f9786" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502507}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "733bc417-d633-5d09-b8d7-6bffa5931366" :question/problem "The vec