int itself. This gives the following diagram.\n\n![](images/a6/a69a9afddf3271e21e7b0a4136a84d4420238af354869085c58d931ac2e045fe.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518817 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d9748db-ff33-5738-9275-47347081811f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/a5/a5ee72ae329a50484d2d6c41983fbcf131500e9f52619d1c6644a63a10e9b92f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518767} {:answer/id #uuid "13ef16eb-1657-5324-8294-4449e71c4000" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/95/9560b790b63b75ce1a0e79e0beb58e0f51693723fdc8ac0642440fd4ad973937.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518770} {:answer/id #uuid "37e994b8-8c59-5ccf-a6e4-81eeb22d9cfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/4e/4e79f6a378556f500223baaa090df75b002cfd83196bd23b748278ef542b0fae.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518779} {:answer/id #uuid "890ee44e-76ba-5143-a748-348d04ac2127" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/2b/2b09ff0226023ff4dc3dc2f8f50f3e0a7882111a64fd4170dafba4f43082d380.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518798} {:answer/id #uuid "922e2ffe-74c1-5bcd-bceb-cbe86b8efa17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/76/76268ad669c8974c2e342d00c31d0545caa1f8d86001b4e30c4142ff7ac6df23.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518806}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518798} :answer-field/id #uuid "48cb5210-6b6f-502e-b04b-51371c35d32a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518782}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "b43bc1bc-dcf4-5470-9387-8faf0f4ffb56" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams represents the vector field $F(x,y)=2 x y\\,i-x^{2}\\,j$ at the indicated points?" :question/worked-solution "We have to sketch the vector field at the points $(-2,\\frac{7}{4}),(1,- \\frac{1}{4}),$ and $(-1,\\frac{7}{4}).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the function $F(x,y)=2 x y\\,i-x^{2}\\,j\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(-2,\\frac{7}{4}) & =\\left((2)(-2)\\left(\\frac{7}{4}\\right)\\right)\\,i+\\left((-1)(-2)^{2}\\right)\\,j=-7\\,i-4\\,j \\\\ F(1,- \\frac{1}{4}) & =\\left((2)(1)\\left(- \\frac{1}{4}\\right)\\right)\\,i+\\left((-1)(1)^{2}\\right)\\,j=-\\frac{1}{2}\\,i-j \\\\ F(-1,\\frac{7}{4}) & =\\left((2)(-1)\\left(\\frac{7}{4}\\right)\\right)\\,i+\\left((-1)(-1)^{2}\\right)\\,j=-\\frac{7}{2}\\,i-j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now draw our vectors. At each point, we draw the vector associated with that point, placing the tail end of the vector on the point itself. This gives the following diagram.\n\n![](images/2b/2b09ff0226023ff4dc3dc2f8f50f3e0a7882111a64fd4170dafba4f43082d380.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518818 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04b689a3-39ce-59dd-8039-cf17d3a57d17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/98/987e9aabd76d28c679efb27b92a2536d103e99eb3f915e6731ec37c56286876f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518764} {:answer/id #uuid "27ad4c1e-99ab-58dd-85d9-2307786676a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/fc/fc92738151b6a9f4c35708a3f911287a739b7f43366f3bb18c888ca4758ac4c2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518777} {:answer/id #uuid "56105024-507d-5779-8bfb-522422369448" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/2d/2d5356db4c62ed3cd1b0fd068f5d16b8ef6a3b8750011ca37ca3657ed2eaab28.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518786} {:answer/id #uuid "94538c99-4a36-5413-b710-fcab9dfdd249" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/e3/e3540bee55bf4207205efc609a695d4222c7707e614c86bfa8cb50b22b524d5d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518809} {:answer/id #uuid "9cd868e0-9e5d-5768-8b1a-bb8fe5d92407" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/ed/ed2c4c2be8527c466b58b3c56d15559161e05dccdbcaaaf380320347f367bc47.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518812}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518764} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c4be32b-ebec-539c-b41e-ace6fb5e23bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518800}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b5efd26b-a36e-5669-8d57-24827ceb919a" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams represents the vector field $F(x,y)=2 x y\\,i-2 x^{2}\\,j$ at the indicated points?" :question/worked-solution "We have to sketch the vector field at the points $(1,- \\frac{1}{2}),(-1,\\frac{3}{2}),$ and $(1,\\frac{1}{2}).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the function $F(x,y)=2 x y\\,i-2 x^{2}\\,j\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1,- \\frac{1}{2}) & =\\left((2)(1)\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\right)\\,i+\\left((-2)(1)^{2}\\right)\\,j=-i-2\\,j \\\\ F(-1,\\frac{3}{2}) & =\\left((2)(-1)\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)\\right)\\,i+\\left((-2)(-1)^{2}\\right)\\,j=-3\\,i-2\\,j \\\\ F(1,\\frac{1}{2}) & =\\left((2)(1)\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\right)\\,i+\\left((-2)(1)^{2}\\right)\\,j=i-2\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now draw our vectors. At each point, we draw the vector associated with that point, placing the tail end of the vector on the point itself. This gives the following diagram.\n\n![](images/98/987e9aabd76d28c679efb27b92a2536d103e99eb3f915e6731ec37c56286876f.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518908 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10c25e88-eda6-5994-8669-2fc4e8989223" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{80}\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518907} {:answer/id #uuid "2938687d-5d55-5245-8c65-6f9840dccd9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "160\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518914} {:answer/id #uuid "3f0938ab-55ed-5367-8d20-ae9cdfd95ae8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "80\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518920} {:answer/id #uuid "a3238964-bd1d-5761-80d6-d8671006ef6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6400\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518951} {:answer/id #uuid "b76da343-223a-5697-a37a-50a8d039196b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "40\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518960}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518920} :answer-field/id #uuid "f13aea66-5851-5988-acfe-308733165daa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518972}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "14ceb78e-322f-54a1-9174-9de018a820b6" :question/problem "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(-1,2)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}\\longrightarrow\\begin{bmatrix}2 u v^{3}\\\\3 u^{2} + v^{2}\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))\\approx\\left|\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|\\cdot\\underbrace{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial u}&\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial v}\\\\\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial u}&\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial v}\\end{vmatrix}\\\\& =\\begin{vmatrix}2 v^{3}&6 u v^{2}\\\\6 u&2 v\\end{vmatrix}\\\\& =(2 v^{3})\\cdot (2 v)-(6 u v^{2})\\cdot (6 u)\\\\& =- 36 u^{2} v^{2} + 4 v^{4}\\\\& =- 4 v^{2} \\left(3 u - v\\right) \\left(3 u + v\\right)\\\\\\left.\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|_{(-1,2)} & =\\left(- 4 v^{2} \\left(3 u - v\\right) \\left(3 u + v\\right)\\right)\\big|_{u=-1,v=2}\\\\& =- 4 (2)^{2} \\left(3 (-1) - (2)\\right) \\left(3 (-1) + (2)\\right)\\\\& =-80\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & \\approx|-80|\\cdot\\delta A\\\\ & =80\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518915 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68183119-0e35-5d48-af62-a8b0b531100a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "192\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518936} {:answer/id #uuid "6abf04e2-7547-5fd6-adf1-679bbe9324da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{96}\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518939} {:answer/id #uuid "a3594f26-df2d-522d-8678-6bd28bc24f8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9216\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518952} {:answer/id #uuid "b0631b4b-2af0-51ae-9938-eed818a10498" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "48\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518957} {:answer/id #uuid "d956c4c8-a269-5eba-9d74-d31be57b55d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "96\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518965}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518965} :answer-field/id #uuid "d765db19-5dd7-5fc5-8884-f5f88ec83632" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518964}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2f65179e-ed0f-5b0a-a190-a9cd8645ec56" :question/problem "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(-3,-1)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}\\longrightarrow\\begin{bmatrix}3 u v^{2}\\\\u^{2} + 2 v^{2}\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))\\approx\\left|\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|\\cdot\\underbrace{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial u}&\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial v}\\\\\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial u}&\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial v}\\end{vmatrix}\\\\& =\\begin{vmatrix}3 v^{2}&6 u v\\\\2 u&4 v\\end{vmatrix}\\\\& =(3 v^{2})\\cdot (4 v)-(6 u v)\\cdot (2 u)\\\\& =- 12 u^{2} v + 12 v^{3}\\\\& =- 12 v \\left(u - v\\right) \\left(u + v\\right)\\\\\\left.\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|_{(-3,-1)} & =\\left(- 12 v \\left(u - v\\right) \\left(u + v\\right)\\right)\\big|_{u=-3,v=-1}\\\\& =- 12 (-1) \\left(- (-1) + (-3)\\right) \\left((-1) + (-3)\\right)\\\\& =96\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & \\approx|96|\\cdot\\delta A\\\\ & =96\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
